{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`import rebar` callers get a return value, not a terminal, so the first-class way to raise a\nnon-fatal warning is Python's dedicated **`warnings`** subsystem (not `logging`, which the\nbrainstorm rejected). This story emits a `warnings.warn` of a dedicated category from\nsingle-ticket library functions when the detector fires. Depends on the detector\n(`cross_session_warning_for`, merged) and the reducer clearing (merged): a ticket not\n`in_progress` has no holder, so the detector returns `None` and nothing is emitted.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a new module `src/rebar/_lib_warn.py` defining `class CrossSessionWarning(UserWarning)`\nand a best-effort helper\n`emit_cross_session_warning(ticket_id, *, repo_root=None, stacklevel=3)`; re-export the\ncategory as `rebar.CrossSessionWarning` from the package so callers can filter/escalate it\nwith stdlib filters. The module also exposes a `suppress_cross_session_warning()` context\nmanager (holds the same guard) so an outer surface that already advises can stop the library\nchannel from doubling it (see Surface layering).\n\nThe helper mirrors the CLI's `_maybe_warn_cross_session` (`src/rebar/_cli/_execute.py`): it\ncalls the merged detector `cross_session_warning_for(ticket_id, repo_root=repo_root)` and,\non a non-`None` string, calls `warnings.warn(msg, CrossSessionWarning, stacklevel=stacklevel)`;\non `None` it does nothing. Two properties are load-bearing:\n\n- **Best-effort — never breaks the call.** The whole body is wrapped in\n  `try/except Exception: pass` (the detector's state read can fail on corrupt/absent/locked\n  state); the library operation always proceeds and no warning is emitted on failure.\n- **Re-entrancy-guarded.** The merged detector (`src/rebar/_commands/cross_session.py`)\n  itself calls public `rebar._lib_reads.show_ticket`, so a naive emit on `show_ticket` would\n  recurse. A module-level `contextvars.ContextVar` (`_EMITTING`, default `False`) makes the\n  helper a no-op while an emit is already in progress: it returns if set, else sets it, runs,\n  and resets in `finally`. So the detector's internal read emits nothing and exactly one\n  warning fires per top-level call. The detector is **not** modified. `stacklevel=3`\n  attributes the warning to the caller of the public function.\n\nEach single-ticket public entry point calls\n`emit_cross_session_warning(ticket_id, repo_root=repo_root)` **before** returning (and, for\nwrites, before the mutation, so the holder is read pre-mutation — matching CLI/MCP). **No\nreturn type changes.** Functions covered, at their definition sites (public names from\n`src/rebar/__init__.py`):\n\n- Reads — `_lib_reads.py`: `show_ticket`, `deps`.\n- Writes — `_lib_writes.py`: `transition`, `reopen`.\n- Mutations — `_lib_mutations.py`: `comment`, `edit_ticket` (public name is `edit_ticket`,\n  not `edit`), `link`, `unlink`, `tag`, `untag`, `archive`.\n- Gates — `_lib_gates.py`: `set_file_impact`, `declare_no_file_impact`, `clarity_check`,\n  `check_ac`. The CLI allowlist warns on `check-ac`, `clarity-check`, `set-file-impact`;\n  `declare_no_file_impact` is the library counterpart of the CLI's `set-file-impact --none`,\n  so it is covered. `quality_check` is **out of scope** — absent from the CLI allowlist and\n  deferred on MCP (S4).\n\n`link`/`unlink` take two endpoints (`id1, id2, relation`); the warning is computed for the\n**primary endpoint `id1`** only, matching CLI (S3) and MCP (S4). Bulk reads (`list_tickets`,\n`search`, `ready`, `next_batch`) do **not** warn. `claim` is excluded: it raises\n`ConcurrencyError` on an `in_progress` ticket before any warning path.\n### Surface layering (single-emit dedup)\n\nThe CLI and MCP surfaces call these same library functions, so a naive library emit doubles\nthe advisory each already carries (CLI stderr `WARN:`; MCP `cross_session_warning` field).\nThe dedup keeps exactly one advisory per operation per surface:\n\n- **CLI** (`src/rebar/_cli/_execute.py`) — `execute()` runs `_maybe_warn_cross_session` (the\n  allowlist single source) **and** the handler dispatch inside\n  `suppress_cross_session_warning()`, so the library `CrossSessionWarning` (including the\n  detector's read during detection) is suppressed; the CLI's `WARN:` line is the only CLI\n  advisory.\n- **MCP** (`src/rebar/mcp_server.py`) — `build_server()` installs a process-wide\n  `filterwarnings(\"ignore\", CrossSessionWarning)`, so the response field is the only MCP\n  advisory in the running server.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_lib_warn.py` (**new**) — `CrossSessionWarning(UserWarning)`, best-effort\n  re-entrancy-guarded `emit_cross_session_warning`, and `suppress_cross_session_warning`.\n- `src/rebar/__init__.py` — re-export `CrossSessionWarning` (import + `__all__`).\n- `src/rebar/_lib_reads.py` — emit in `show_ticket`, `deps`.\n- `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py` — emit in `transition`, `reopen` (before the mutation).\n- `src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py` — emit in `comment`, `edit_ticket`, `link` (`id1`),\n  `unlink` (`id1`), `tag`, `untag`, `archive` (before the mutation).\n- `src/rebar/_lib_gates.py` — emit in `set_file_impact`, `declare_no_file_impact`,\n  `clarity_check`, `check_ac`. `quality_check` out of scope (see Approach).\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_execute.py` — hold `suppress_cross_session_warning()` across detection +\n  dispatch so the library channel never doubles the CLI `WARN:` line.\n- `src/rebar/mcp_server.py` — `build_server()` ignores `CrossSessionWarning` process-wide.\n- `docs/reuse-surface.md` — document `rebar.CrossSessionWarning` and single-ticket emission.\n- `tests/unit/test_cross_session_lib.py` (**new**) — the library-surface oracle.\n\n## Testing\n\nTier: **in-process unit test** with stdlib `warnings` capture (`pytest.warns` /\n`catch_warnings(record=True)`). Real temporary tracker; acting session via `REBAR_SESSION_ID`\n(monkeypatch). Claim as holder A, then act as B.\n\n- B vs A-held: `show_ticket` and `comment` each emit one warning naming A; write applies.\n- Write + two-endpoint: `transition` and `link` (holder A on `id1`) each emit one for `id1`.\n- Negative control (same session A): none. Bulk (`list_tickets`/`ready` as B): none.\n- Unset `REBAR_SESSION_ID`: none. Category is `isinstance(..., CrossSessionWarning)`.\n- Re-entrancy: exactly one per top-level `show_ticket`.\n- Best-effort: monkeypatch `cross_session_warning_for` to raise -> call returns, no warning.\n- CLI dedup: merged `test_cross_session_cli.py` asserts one `WARN:` per command (RED on a\n  double-emit). Defect-seeded: negate `msg is not None` / wrong endpoint -> RED.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `rebar.show_ticket(<id>)` and `rebar.comment(<id>, ...)`, as B vs an A-held ticket, each\n  emit exactly one `rebar.CrossSessionWarning` naming holder `A` (`pytest.warns` under\n  `make test`); the `comment` write still applies.\n- [x] `rebar.transition(<id>, \"in_progress\", \"closed\")` and `rebar.link(<id1>, <id2>, ...)`\n  (endpoint `id1`), as B vs A-held `id1`, each emit one `CrossSessionWarning` naming `A`.\n- [x] Same-session A negative control emits none (`catch_warnings(record=True)`).\n- [x] `rebar.list_tickets()` and `rebar.ready()` as B emit none for A's `in_progress` ticket.\n- [x] With `REBAR_SESSION_ID` unset, `rebar.show_ticket(<id>)` emits none.\n- [x] The emitted warning `isinstance(..., rebar.CrossSessionWarning)` subclassing\n  `UserWarning`.\n- [x] Exactly one `CrossSessionWarning` per top-level `rebar.show_ticket(<id>)` despite the\n  detector's internal read (recorded count for that category is 1).\n- [x] Best-effort: when `cross_session_warning_for` raises, the library call returns normally\n  and emits no `CrossSessionWarning` (monkeypatch-to-raise).\n- [x] Single-emit dedup: a warning CLI command (e.g. `link`) writes exactly one `WARN:` line,\n  not doubled by the library channel (`test_cross_session_cli.py` `count(...) == 1`).\n- [x] `docs/reuse-surface.md` documents `rebar.CrossSessionWarning` and single-ticket\n  emission (`grep -n \"CrossSessionWarning\" docs/reuse-surface.md` matches)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787904025104568001,"uuid":"713aa38d-6325-42dc-aa32-a70ec4eefb65"}